{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/golden_single_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:58:21.951795Z","id":"d5d25c036575c8d79a42b36bcd0ff037ca6859b8afc4a3eef1dcc021b6005f5b","body":{"detail":"With first-take ownership (spec 2026-10-08 M23), the collection's takes make the fixture's live agent the owner of the threads it is delivered, and GET .../threads then carries owner {handle, live, name, person} (spec section 19 item 6 lists owner as an expected additive field). Compared with the committed fixtures/single-owner-21.golden.json after removing every owner key, the regenerated golden is equal. The committed golden was not rewritten: whether to regenerate it now or let plan Task 25's comparison expect the field is open.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":877},"end":{"line":890},"content_hash":"e380f23f39bcb646c8d62dafd110ba3cb4e77b3435c48da23a69a1ad4d48704c"},"summary":"Regenerating the single-owner golden adds an owner field to 36 raw thread views; it is otherwise identical","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/golden_single_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T16:47:38.362437Z","id":"109c814e8ac8b1e516d72bbf9ab9c4761630d3fc8e96a10da5cf0b40bcad63d0","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Ruled by the coordinator in the Task 15 review: the golden holds when it is identical once every owner key is removed (spec 2026-10-08 section 19 item 6 expects owner); the committed golden stays. Checked again at 1f0f12a: equal without owner, 36 owner values added.","supersedes":"d5d25c036575c8d79a42b36bcd0ff037ca6859b8afc4a3eef1dcc021b6005f5b","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted_content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:58:52.364409Z","id":"5f44f1de989e3332d4a8270b7d9e8d6e460fe432255b2bed2361b1fc464efce3","body":{"detail":"the_content_tests_pass_when_content_io_needs_an_executor reruns api_artifacts, api_content, api_assets, api_threads and the api_live* modules with CLAX_TEST_SERVER_CONTENT=deferred, skipping the tests that read or change the home files or call synchronous store methods themselves. A stale skip name skips nothing and a new such test fails the rerun, which is loud; its >100 threshold only catches an empty filter. Content routes outside those modules (for example docs, approvals) are not rerun.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":161},"end":{"line":202},"content_hash":"f198c5e6916be4111196ec404f505223ad4ff56dca8f14c72e527349c488b94d"},"summary":"The Deferred-content rerun skips ten tests by name and adds about 5 s to the server suite; a renamed or new file-layout test needs the list kept by hand","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:37:11.638796Z","id":"6dd9b4184d83df959232bb6b344eaeaa9fc421b9186650e7972ccaf426db8927","body":{"detail":"Mutation runs against crates/clax-server/tests (api_people, api_agent_auth, api_sessions, api_grants): sessionless_narrow keeping only the first narrowing (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs, `Some(a) => a`) and proved_row refreshing a proved row of another harness (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:352) both pass every test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1281},"end":{"line":1333},"content_hash":"3e044e1505a04649ae16a0975ec1470709302b20b947a74e2fed155dd94e7268"},"suggested_fix":"Narrow two sessions to different locations and check a session-less request gets neither's excess; register with a proof of a claude session as codex and check a new row is made.","summary":"No test has two narrowed sessions, or a proof of a session of another harness","tags":["review","test-gap","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:20.904951Z","id":"af8904b3c8011df4d0be08b5ca5635d3f9b1ca350dba70a8e87b8520764d4f22","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:903f2670","summary":"api_people::every_live_narrowing_binds_a_request_naming_no_session narrows two sessions in both orders (catches the first-narrowing-only mutation); a_nested_agent_proving_its_parents_session_gets_its_own proves a session of another harness (a new codex row, not the proved claude one); the PID fallback and the join's wait are pinned by the tests named on 5d0c97a9 and 64fd9bb2. All eleven fix-round mutations are caught (target/t19a/mutations2.txt).","supersedes":"6dd9b4184d83df959232bb6b344eaeaa9fc421b9186650e7972ccaf426db8927","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:05:31.657850Z","id":"d494907231a2d1935b8081788e7979574f0e7397cb8df554ac5b33d7d50c350b","body":{"detail":"Two mutations survive api_approvals::, api_threads::, shell_boot:: and api_events:: (83 tests). (1) In keep_approvers (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:583-588), Handles::Of(Some(p)) keeps approver for every connected person. (2) In boot.rs:196, the boot payload uses Handles::All for LAN viewers and anonymous callers. whose_approval_a_thread_waits_for_reaches_only_the_people_concerned asks only the owner, the approver, the author, a LAN viewer and no cookie, although its doc comment promises 'nor a connected person the thread does not concern'. Also, a decide_request that does not re-announce its thread (crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1959-1963) is caught only by a_declined_comment_leaves_its_thread_waiting_for_nothing hanging until nextest ends it at 120 s. Bound that event wait.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2456},"end":{"line":2501},"content_hash":"dfadd941db10671133605410494e0f24a27d6f75ae13bb49301e7d238232a7fc"},"summary":"No test covers the approver rule for a connected person a thread does not concern, or for the boot payload","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.888794Z","id":"ae90aa83576fb59f9ba012d5b2a23ebcf555d5ec26cfa9bb6a7a51ed2b5f8efc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:86cc3ac0","summary":"whose_approval_a_thread_waits_for_reaches_only_the_people_concerned now asks Mia, a connected person the thread does not concern, and reads the boot payload for every caller; event waits are bounded (within, 10 s). Evidence: three mutations each fail a test: Handles::Of(Some(p)) keeping the full state for every person (whose_approval_..., Mia), boot using Handles::All for everyone (whose_approval_..., Lucy's boot), and decide_request not re-announcing (a_declined_thread_..., held_state wait fails in 10 s).","supersedes":"d494907231a2d1935b8081788e7979574f0e7397cb8df554ac5b33d7d50c350b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:30:59.641540Z","id":"a5c6889e1b5c9c0eaa0a3f6dfec7c2b08956b39d250f68a48f56e4d571e43b0a","body":{"detail":"Mutations run with the api_approvals, api_threads, shell_boot, api_events and api_inbox integration tests (104 tests). M6: concerned() (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:491-505) skips the thread's authors, so held_state reaches only the owner's inbox topic: all pass. M9: states_for gives Handles::All full(false), so the owner's own approval never reads mine ('waiting for your approval'): all pass. The tests hear held_state on the owner's topic only, and assert no mine for the owner only where Sam approves. Add a held_state read on Mia's (an author's) and Sam's (the approver's) inbox topics, and a thread waiting for the owner's approval read by the owner's browser with mine: true.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2471},"end":{"line":2635},"content_hash":"3a530416ffb32bdba7a4327552cfe89e361fc6ec4fe295a2b3d222256324a88d"},"summary":"Two mutations of the held-state rules survive: held_state reaching only the owner, and the owner's browser never reading mine","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.441755Z","id":"f52305d10af72a7703be0ffe62cbfd9bae4f92951fda88284c450c644a2124a0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:628b724a","summary":"Fixed by new tests: api_approvals::the_approver_reads_its_own_decisions (Sam's decline reaches Sam's own stream with mine: true, and Mia's and the owner's) catches M6 (a decision reaches the owner alone); api_approvals::the_owner_reads_every_rows_state_and_mine_for_its_own_approval (the owner reads mine: true on Mia's thread to its agent) catches M7 (the owner never reads mine). Each mutation was restored by rewriting the file's bytes.","supersedes":"a5c6889e1b5c9c0eaa0a3f6dfec7c2b08956b39d250f68a48f56e4d571e43b0a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_gateway.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:49:30.468062Z","id":"8ece94f2fbd3b2a3cf18cad2caaf0beb6d1f703224d8a2222d0ec4bad7b22773","body":{"detail":"The case asks /api/artifacts/{hid}/approves-first with `tid`, a thread of the live page, so the handler's thread_of answers 404 whatever the gateway does. With the rule in crates/clax-server/src/extension.rs:238 changed to Rule::Any, `cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_gateway` still passes (12 passed); only the unit table the_allowlist_names_each_route_and_the_artifact_it_needs_live fails.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":294},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"21e1c1ea62544ffdf9a9f1bb153dbf0886508b958631a37f7249d0338de4d19e"},"suggested_fix":"Make a thread on the published (non-live) artifact `hid` and ask approves-first for it: 404 from the gateway, 200 without it.","summary":"The approves-first refusal case would pass without the gateway's live-page check","tags":["review","test","task:23","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_gateway.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:05:29.985434Z","id":"19f536a3c6b2e4142a70e651e632f400bab5d5000df5977f7f9a1596d4a5b416","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:21d2a440","summary":"everything_else_is_refused now asks approves-first on the published page about that page's own thread (htid), so the handler would answer 200; only the gateway's live-page rule refuses it. Mutation: with the rule changed to Rule::Any the test fails; restored, api_gateway passes (12/12).","supersedes":"8ece94f2fbd3b2a3cf18cad2caaf0beb6d1f703224d8a2222d0ec4bad7b22773","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_timeout.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T13:04:52.464585Z","id":"1be89cf758c09e72d95aa30d0816bc005be1634c76dbf96ac920e4c82c5e29dd","body":{"detail":"Failure seen once: //crates/clax-server:integration__3 at commit 31b71b26, load about 6, assets upload answered 408 'request exceeded 2s' at api_timeout.rs:158 (expected 201). Three reruns (--runs_per_test=3) passed. Each request carries a 500 ms delay header against publish_timeout = 2 s, so any upload slower than 1.5 s under load fails. A wider timeout (or an injected clock for the timeout layer) would keep the test from depending on the machine's speed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":99},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"496b99fe92f67149664e5e8c9f732fb62dc0fe0e2a078f7286f57ea0928b665b"},"summary":"The publish-timeout test can fail on a slow machine: three uploads must each finish within a 2 s wall-clock timeout","tags":["flaky","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted_content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:21:31.816599Z","id":"7f8dfab537761624b025de18c8f7137c3b05e75e142056029869b83d5d00f0b5","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The test moved to crates/clax-server/tests/common/deferred.rs, which every split test target compiles; the concern is recorded again there, with what the split changes.","supersedes":"5f44f1de989e3332d4a8270b7d9e8d6e460fe432255b2bed2361b1fc464efce3","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/deferred.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.844982Z","id":"4df6b70c7620a5595755894e7aacd6ddb2c73654f6082d34b7411a02cd96a1cf","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/tests/common/deferred.rs:46-97, record 92c3be13.\n\nthe_content_tests_pass_when_content_io_needs_an_executor reruns, of api_artifacts, api_content, api_assets, api_threads and the api_live* modules, those this test binary holds (all under Cargo; under Bazel, those its integration__N target was dealt, crates/clax-server/BUILD.bazel) with CLAX_TEST_SERVER_CONTENT=deferred, skipping the tests that read or change the home files or call synchronous store methods themselves. A stale skip name skips nothing and a new such test fails the rerun, which is loud. Under Cargo the >100 threshold catches an empty filter; under Bazel each held module must have one passing test in the rerun. holds() names each module by its clax_split cfg, so a module added to MODULES without a holds() arm is never rerun under Bazel. Content routes outside those modules (for example docs, approvals) are not rerun. Moved with the test from crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted_content.rs (record 5f44f1de989e3332d4a8270b7d9e8d6e460fe432255b2bed2361b1fc464efce3).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:217836344261c10bd08dc555b813e6df2823eb7c","span":{"start":{"line":46},"end":{"line":97},"content_hash":"569d77cbd123cd3f8ffa22e89e01e90fb12092dc5cf8113b12b5ec77ee5c7181"},"summary":"The Deferred-content rerun skips eleven tests by name and adds seconds to each server test target that holds a rerun module; a renamed or new file-layout test needs the list kept by hand, and a new module whose content routes should rerun needs adding to MODULES and holds()","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:52:20.537113Z","id":"4d403064ab05092a6986360a1ff5da3310fbfb3d70b49e6c6dd2de15348a3348","body":{"detail":"tests/deferred.rs reruns, on deferred content, the content test modules of the test target it is compiled into, reading that target's clax_split cfg, so it must be a module of crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs, in every target, not a library. The MCP and public Clax helpers it sat beside in tests/common moved to clax-testkit (mcp.rs, remotes.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":130},"end":{"line":130},"content_hash":"55653b2a3989f67b681b525ef79b5ab056f03ac86a3a755b78d5e92572e4b2c1"},"summary":"Put the deferred-content rerun in clax-testkit with the other test helpers","tags":["tests","layout","revisit:Bazel's split targets pass the modules they hold another way","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T15:12:24.892970Z","id":"1c02e0439f8611a55f0e2c5b805935dfe2531b2b6cbff4f1b4452c4de2327147","body":{"detail":"Failure: in one run of scripts/quality_gates.sh, cargo nextest failed api_linked::an_open_copy_holds_one_poll_there_however_often_the_sync_wakes at line 1211, assert_eq!(question_waiters(&rqid), 1): left 0, right 1, after five backstop wakes and sleeper.wait_for(BACKSTOP, 1). The same test passed alone natively (1.0 s) and in both Bazel runs of //crates/clax-server:integration__*. A sync wake that ends the remote poll and starts the next leaves a moment with no waiter.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1199},"end":{"line":1211},"content_hash":"e6dc063f675a42bfb961f462ba0419566aceba390032a7473f8a0d84053fcdf0"},"suggested_fix":"Wait until the count is 1 (or assert that it never exceeds 1 across the wakes) rather than reading it once.","summary":"The one-poll test reads the remote's waiter count at one instant, between polls it can be 0","tags":["tests","flaky","linked","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:13:49.995554Z","id":"57d9b52540a1fbe71903cdd3726993b6d112d883ab7b40d67fd365c331252abb","body":{"detail":"Failure: in 1 of 100 runs of //crates/clax-server:integration__4 (bazel test --runs_per_test=100 --local_test_jobs=12, the six integration targets at once and six CPU-bound processes beside them), line 1097 found linked.answered_there false on a question already answered (answered_via \"shell\", linked.sent true). The other 99 runs passed. The answer and the flag reach the local row apart, and the test reads the row once after the ask returns.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1096},"end":{"line":1097},"content_hash":"c7fad44d4bb1ee98b0eff4e53cdf0b1b3dcf044b6490f60f16ea0fdbcd387511"},"suggested_fix":"Wait until local_question shows answered_there (until(...)), or set the flag in the same write that closes the question.","summary":"a_local_ask_on_a_linked_artifact_is_asked_there_and_answered_from_there can read the local question answered before its answered_there flag is set","tags":["tests","flaky","linked","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_tool_call_ids.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:13:49.995884Z","id":"d549d9cc9ba409985c704ce0ec31c8e3784a8992ecb24f5b25e2c043065ad761","body":{"detail":"Failure: in 1 of 100 runs of //crates/clax-server:integration__4 under the load described on crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs:1096, line 370 got {\"call_id\":null,\"recorded\":true,\"seq\":5} where the publish call's ID was expected. The daemon is no_grace() (CallIdWait with Duration::ZERO), so a report that arrives before the matching call is visible gets none; the test's back-dated event is 120 s before Utc::now(), a wall-clock reference. The other 99 runs passed. Not investigated further.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":348},"end":{"line":371},"content_hash":"6d8a705c757a6f0d3eee28930c98c3310f090bad67bd0376ff6beba330b95915"},"summary":"a_clock_step_back_hides_no_call failed once under heavy load: the hook's report found no call ID","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:14:59.901788Z","id":"e75375fdba5f3bf3066f97cd1ffb253c2553cac7c5a670b7aa74b1b74f8e7ddd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:844c74d2b","summary":"Fixed in 844c74d2b: the test waits for the remote's waiter count to be 1 (TestServer::wait_question_waiters, which answers once the count equals 1) instead of reading it once. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__4 --runs_per_test=100 --local_test_jobs=12 --nocache_test_results, run with the other five integration targets at 100 runs each and six CPU-bound processes beside them: api_linked::an_open_copy_holds_one_poll_there_however_often_the_sync_wakes ... ok in all 100 run logs (grep -l '... ok' over testlogs/crates/clax-server/integration__4/run_*_of_100/test.log: 100; '... FAILED': 0).","supersedes":"1c02e0439f8611a55f0e2c5b805935dfe2531b2b6cbff4f1b4452c4de2327147","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:45:12.360258Z","id":"35f4d20632ac14084abbac761bc318d98439cb22fecb9050ea30c4bb0c847bba","body":{"detail":"Failure: in one run of scripts/quality_gates.sh, cargo nextest failed it at line 1156 (assert_eq!(late(..)[0][\"id\"], qid, \"let go\"): left Null). wait_question_waiters(&qid, 0) returns once the aborted poll is counted gone, which may be before the daemon's handling of that ending makes the answer available to the feedback poll late() reads. Rerun alone it passed natively (just test-native an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll) and in 20 of 20 Bazel runs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1155},"end":{"line":1156},"content_hash":"fcccb7cf0425bb156f3f84259f0ad835713cd911c132254922869bb63a1fa179"},"suggested_fix":"Poll late() until it names qid (with the test kit's until), rather than reading it once after the waiter count drops.","summary":"an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll can find no late answer just after the question poll lets go","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/golden_single_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:22:17.261094Z","id":"67ab75345f8b1c35ae708a5ecd19f83925359e14614045dbce4addf37be13e31","body":{"detail":"The module doc forbids regenerating the golden except on a rebased base at the collector's commit. Asking where the person is adds the keys to question views and poll replies, and clax_core::surface::line to every delivery's text, on every install; without_where_to_ask strips that line only when it is the text's last and the golden lacks it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":872},"end":{"line":941},"content_hash":"035b34d6b1e41736a22a2881bd554319c47dc191cd2f7c8f0fa4d4a7753241ea"},"summary":"The single-owner golden comparison accepts where_to_ask, in_terminal, pulled and thread as additive keys and a final where-to-ask line, rather than regenerating the golden","tags":["revisit:the golden is regenerated on a rebased base","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/golden_single_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:38:49.694620Z","id":"5b02047a10ebcf73489ca2c21efa0df9ff7082f44873e6325230113bc6699f88","body":{"detail":"compare_with_section_19 accepts, only inside a write whose tool is \"ask\" on both sides, a string that moved from <base>/inbox?q=<ULID> to <base>/a/<id> or <base>/a/<id>?thread=<ULID> on the same base (moved_to_its_place; test the_section_19_comparison_allows_an_ask_url_moved_to_its_place_only). The ask result's url names the narrowest place the question shows (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md section 2), so the fixture's three ask writes now name their artifact. The golden (crates/clax-testkit/fixtures/single-owner-21.golden.json) is regenerated only on a rebased base, never to make the comparison pass (module doc), so the change is an allowance here.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":951},"end":{"line":971},"content_hash":"1424f74298d840823bd8741a6fd1336a31f3308314c54f8b6e650a65bdc1638e"},"summary":"Regenerate the single-owner golden instead of accepting an ask URL moved to its place","tags":["revisit:the golden is regenerated on a rebased base, after which the allowance matches nothing and can go","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.594081Z","id":"ba9aa541c2f63aaf204c2119157f850ab491578051801034ac064079abe49259","body":{"detail":"Failure: in one run of scripts/quality_gates.sh, cargo nextest failed it at line 1156 (assert_eq!(late(..)[0][\"id\"], qid, \"let go\"): left Null). wait_question_waiters(&qid, 0) returns once the aborted poll is counted gone, which may be before the daemon's handling of that ending makes the answer available to the feedback poll late() reads. Rerun alone it passed natively (just test-native an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll) and in 20 of 20 Bazel runs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1160},"end":{"line":1161},"content_hash":"fcccb7cf0425bb156f3f84259f0ad835713cd911c132254922869bb63a1fa179"},"suggested_fix":"Poll late() until it names qid (with the test kit's until), rather than reading it once after the waiter count drops.","summary":"an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll can find no late answer just after the question poll lets go","supersedes":"35f4d20632ac14084abbac761bc318d98439cb22fecb9050ea30c4bb0c847bba","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/golden_single_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.616925Z","id":"a0541f35d45fa69a5826fc1f25019313e67fd854f7830793dbedb58d27fc15bc","body":{"detail":"The module doc forbids regenerating the golden except on a rebased base at the collector's commit. Asking where the person is adds the keys to question views and poll replies, and clax_core::surface::line to every delivery's text, on every install; without_where_to_ask strips that line only when it is the text's last and the golden lacks it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":880},"end":{"line":949},"content_hash":"035b34d6b1e41736a22a2881bd554319c47dc191cd2f7c8f0fa4d4a7753241ea"},"summary":"The single-owner golden comparison accepts where_to_ask, in_terminal, pulled and thread as additive keys and a final where-to-ask line, rather than regenerating the golden","supersedes":"67ab75345f8b1c35ae708a5ecd19f83925359e14614045dbce4addf37be13e31","tags":["revisit:the golden is regenerated on a rebased base","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.640339Z","id":"ddb12a1853a862bc2c55a11616e9f2185619f9ad8a2c4bb4b8e746b2844e4c23","body":{"detail":"tests/deferred.rs reruns, on deferred content, the content test modules of the test target it is compiled into, reading that target's clax_split cfg, so it must be a module of crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs, in every target, not a library. The MCP and public Clax helpers it sat beside in tests/common moved to clax-testkit (mcp.rs, remotes.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":132},"end":{"line":132},"content_hash":"55653b2a3989f67b681b525ef79b5ab056f03ac86a3a755b78d5e92572e4b2c1"},"summary":"Put the deferred-content rerun in clax-testkit with the other test helpers","supersedes":"4d403064ab05092a6986360a1ff5da3310fbfb3d70b49e6c6dd2de15348a3348","tags":["tests","layout","revisit:Bazel's split targets pass the modules they hold another way","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_app_session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:02:35.345746Z","id":"7d04d3e3410ab1b8cfc067aa53637413e412fa63dda1af7f4ff852eff9fc271b","body":{"detail":"POST .../threads/<tid>/comments answers 200 with {\"guidance\": GUIDANCE_REPLY} and writes nothing when the thread was not sent to the agent (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:523-525, 454). The assertion at line 72 is `is_success()`, which accepts that 200, and nothing later reads the thread's comments, so a regression that drops the app's agent reply (or routes the send elsewhere) still passes. The app worker's restart recovery decides from these comments (an owner comment with no `author_kind: \"agent\"` comment after it), so the reply's shape is part of what the server must keep.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":94},"content_hash":"b0bfae939aa908ffc816d4dc5281d2acb328810f1b78393a36228165ce77e81c"},"suggested_fix":"Assert the reply's status is 201 and that the thread read at line 87 has a last comment with author_kind \"agent\" and via_harness \"app\".","summary":"The app reply test passes when the reply writes nothing","tags":["review","test-quality","flutter-app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_app_session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:05:51.886069Z","id":"2d08cbfcd895879b4fb5a6e25358310724e1e11a36fd9d58278dcbe880f6aab8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:660fdc49","summary":"app_session_replies_and_resolves_as_the_agent now asserts the reply answers 201, and that the thread's last comment is the reply with author_kind agent and via_harness app, and resolved_by agent:app. With the send_thread call removed the test fails at the 201 assertion (left: 200, the guidance answer); with it, `cargo nextest run -p clax-server -E 'test(/^api_app_session::/)'`: 5 tests run: 5 passed.","supersedes":"7d04d3e3410ab1b8cfc067aa53637413e412fa63dda1af7f4ff852eff9fc271b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_restore.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:13.307902Z","id":"2556b2288c535da1527ecc3d6ab0cca2619a7c261d9c7ccb43f7ef25db87f677","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_restore.rs covers the happy path, stale if_version, unknown version or artifact, missing fields, token, session and the event. Untested: (1) the 400 live_page answer of routes::artifacts::restore (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:716-721); (2) the Conflict that write_version_from raises inside the transaction when another version lands between restore_version's own check and the transaction (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:784-827), testable at the store level by publishing between the two steps or by a store test with a stale `expected`; (3) the audit record a restore writes (kind version.publish, label, note, carried); (4) a publish after a restore carrying the restored version's files and index.html staying at the version root, which pins the new Carry.index branch of write_version_from (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:883).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":279},"content_hash":"017aade347362471b48a3ccba0745286d0aae389394fe26f2ec8843898546b4c"},"summary":"Restore tests leave out the live-page refusal, the in-transaction conflict re-check, the audit record, and a publish that follows a restore","tags":["tests","review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_restore.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:24.147829Z","id":"8edfa1bc3c425cba9ade2734d21cecd6bb8216cf4c18f5051d11a37910962f9d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6598f558","summary":"Added api_restore::a_live_page_cannot_be_restored, api_restore::a_publish_after_a_restore_builds_on_the_restored_files, store::artifacts::tests::a_version_landing_before_the_restore_transaction_is_a_conflict, a_restore_records_its_source_and_only_unchanged_files_as_carried, a_publish_after_a_restore_carries_the_restored_files (index.html at the version root). cargo nextest run --no-fail-fast -p clax-core -p clax-server: 1214 passed; the 1 failure is store::backfill::tests::the_backfill_changes_nothing_but_version_hashes on the uncommitted db_read_grants migration in the working tree, not this change.","supersedes":"2556b2288c535da1527ecc3d6ab0cca2619a7c261d9c7ccb43f7ef25db87f677","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_timeout.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:08:04.385875Z","id":"dbec06f8329eee8e71fe0e82081dc7f87ed3a0d83d70a36557f1266d59e6f3ca","body":{"detail":"The test sets publish_timeout to 2 s and sends four requests each delayed 500 ms by x-clax-test-delay-ms, so it asserts the real handler (publish, versions, asset upload) finishes within 1.5 s of wall clock. In a full 'cargo nextest run -p clax-core -p clax-server' on 2026-10-13 it failed at line 157 with {\"error\":{\"code\":\"timeout\",\"message\":\"request exceeded 2s\"}} (1229 passed, 1 failed); run alone it passed. AGENTS.md forbids wall-clock budgets in functional tests. The routing to the publish timeout group could be pinned by giving the fast group a short timeout and the publish group a generous one (for example 60 s) with the same delay, so only the 408 versus 201 split is asserted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":97},"end":{"line":158},"content_hash":"87ebfdb7adea28cd73a100a8a77be0839765ff5aa1e0c14c3f2e32b767e2f394"},"summary":"publish_routes_run_under_the_publish_timeout is a wall-clock budget that fails under load","tags":["review","flaky","review:R4","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/core_start.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.461069Z","id":"6c7ee5f4f5f148836925f89ae56a7ac078ac53382bbfc94cd13bb456d9c2bec0","body":{"detail":"clax_store::Store takes no exclusive lock on the database (no locking_mode=EXCLUSIVE or file lock on the home's db; crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs), so a second Core::start on the same home succeeds while the first core's store, tasks and journal still run. The test therefore pins nothing about Core::stop, which serve() now relies on for its whole teardown (crates/clax-server/src/serve.rs:449).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"6bdc348b52e07f6e56f8c0fcca1e766e05b14f7280245ce95b658bcad3cf4e28"},"suggested_fix":"Assert what stop does: e.g. the store answers an error after stop (a Store::call after shutdown), the journal's segment is closed, or a background task's handle is finished.","summary":"stopping_a_core_closes_its_store_so_another_opens_the_home passes whether or not Core::stop closes the store","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:18:40.365459Z","id":"7f9cdd482c3b6ff6dc47ece0a5cf5e4eafa1f8905cf58972d9a67f0ac497ec6c","body":{"detail":"an_outside_agents_bad_icon_is_refused checks the MCP text for invalid_icon and the sentence; publish::tests::a_bad_icon_refuses_the_publish checks CoreError::InvalidIcon. Nothing asserts that POST /api/artifacts (or /versions, /api/drafts) answers 400 with `rule` beside the message (crates/clax-http/src/error.rs CoreError::InvalidIcon arm), so dropping that line passes every test. The six model-written icons in apps/clax_app/test/fixtures/icons are checked only by icon_svg_test.dart; they pass the core today (run through icon::problem) but are not among the shared vectors, so a stricter core rule could refuse the icons the app's agent actually writes without a failing Rust test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":344},"end":{"line":373},"content_hash":"91ba09882b8602ed98f5f75325691a8458e7b6c3bc29a3b33666b0819abff2a6"},"suggested_fix":"Assert body.rule == \"element\" in the MCP case (or an HTTP case over POST /api/artifacts/<id>/versions), and copy the six sample icons into crates/clax-core/tests/fixtures/icons as ok-sample-*.svg.","summary":"No test reads the invalid_icon error's `rule` field, which docs/contract.md promises, and the app's sample icons are run by the Dart check only","tags":["review","icon","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/core_start.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.528748Z","id":"5f78c41a74868136ef0bcd395863c345ecd473431d00a3448df8714e02404ebe","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6762a986b","summary":"Fixed in 6762a986b: stopping_a_core_closes_its_store_and_ends_its_streams asserts the stopped core's store refuses Store::call and its shutdown watch is true. It fails ('a stopped core's store refuses calls') with Core::stop's store.shutdown() replaced by a drop, and passes as committed.","supersedes":"6c7ee5f4f5f148836925f89ae56a7ac078ac53382bbfc94cd13bb456d9c2bec0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:35:11.900410Z","id":"8d5db04542d756da20a75f5c17fc178d261568b10bb2ced78f223eec0773bfec","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fdfbdf9a6","summary":"api_artifacts::a_bad_icon_is_invalid_icon_with_its_rule (POST /api/artifacts and /versions) and the MCP test assert error.rule; both failed with the rule line removed from crates/clax-http/src/error.rs and pass with it. The six sample icons are ok-sample-*.svg vectors, held equal to apps/clax_app/test/fixtures/icons by icon_fixtures_test.dart.","supersedes":"7f9cdd482c3b6ff6dc47ece0a5cf5e4eafa1f8905cf58972d9a67f0ac497ec6c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:10:12.310158Z","id":"cba037ca69165e2416e83d043c77431b2af7786d1121bd1efa7d1777d896a70e","body":{"detail":"The question poll (crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs, the handler of GET /api/sessions/{id}/questions/{qid}) takes its hold (QuestionWaiters::hold, counted by wait_question_waiters) before its loop's first store read. The test waits for one waiter and closes the question in the store; when the close lands before that first read, the poll reads the declined question, takes it and answers it, so the later late() after ask.abort() finds no answer and 'let go' fails with Null. Measured at 15b06ff9d^ (before any jobs route): bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:all --test_arg=api_questions::an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll --runs_per_test=30 failed 5 of 30 runs of integration__6; with an eprintln of ask.is_finished() before the abort, 8 of 9 failing runs had the poll already answered.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1131},"end":{"line":1160},"content_hash":"c0334c082ea901a4bbdd6f258ecdc98304eca99e9239b4be54d66a3d51d7ac85"},"suggested_fix":"Have the test wait until the poll has parked (a debug waiter count taken after the first read), or close the question before the poll starts and assert on the hold some other way.","summary":"an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll races the poll's first read","tags":["review","flaky","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
